WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.510
So, let's quickly talk about a question

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:03.870
that I receive quite a lot from our

00:00:03.880 --> 00:00:05.630
community members, which is how many

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:07.990
skills is actually too many. And my

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.590
answer to this is actually really

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.230
simple. My view is as long as it doesn't

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.430
confuse you or it doesn't confuse

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.910
Claude, then it's most likely fine. And

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.390
the good news about it is that as you

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.590
continue to build up your skill library,

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:22.070
it's actually really easy to audit

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.110
because Claude code by itself can do

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.350
that on its own. Because remember,

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.110
skills are all just text files, it's all

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:29.310
just code and assets that Claude code

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.030
can parse through at the speed of light.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.990
So, if you just copy a prompt like this,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.150
send it to Claude, then that is one

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:37.670
simple way for you to audit your skills,

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:39.430
list any that overlap or could be

00:00:39.440 --> 00:00:41.350
merged, and to give you suggestions on

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:43.790
which to keep, cut, or combine. So, it's

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:45.950
literally that easy. And so, that's why

00:00:45.960 --> 00:00:47.550
I think for the most part, you don't

00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.230
really have to worry about having too

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.070
many skills because with a simple audit

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:52.950
like this, you can clean it up in like

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.790
less than 30 minutes. Now, one important

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.830
thing to consider is let's say you're on

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:58.910
the Pro plan, which has more limited

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:01.470
tokens versus plan, then if you really

00:01:01.480 --> 00:01:03.670
want to maximize your token usage, it

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.509
might be worth cleaning up your skills

00:01:05.519 --> 00:01:07.350
just for that. For you to do a quick

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:09.310
audit if that's a problem for you, you

00:01:09.320 --> 00:01:12.310
can just type in /context on a new and

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.030
fresh Claude code session, and with

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:16.550
this, you'll be able to see exactly how

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.870
many tokens are preloaded in each

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.390
session. So, you can see if I type in

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:23.310
any chat message in that Claude code

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:25.390
session, immediately, I will consume

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.470
around 27,000 tokens in my usage. Now,

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:30.030
what's great about this view is that

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:32.230
Claude code actually gives you a view of

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.190
how much tokens your skill descriptions

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:37.070
are consuming. So, you can see right

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:39.710
now, I have something like 180 skills in

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.830
total that is consuming around 13,700

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.510
tokens, which in the broader scheme of

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:46.150
things is not a lot. Because remember,

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:48.470
Opus 4 8 has 1 million tokens in its

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.870
context window. So, that is minuscule

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:53.110
compared to what is available to you.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:54.590
Now, if you want to see just how much

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.150
your pre-injected system prompts are

00:01:57.160 --> 00:01:59.750
consuming out of your total usage, it's

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:01.910
actually quite a simple exercise. What

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:03.910
you just need to do is to go to account

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:05.670
and usage, which you can find in the

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.230
commands list there, or just type in

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:08.870
{slash} usage as we have discussed

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:10.469
previously. And if you take a look at

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:12.310
your weekly rate limit here, which is

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:14.190
the one that most people hit anyway,

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.550
right now you can see I'm at 6%.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.710
Granted, this is in the max plan, right?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.710
But if I just type a test here, what

00:02:20.720 --> 00:02:23.390
that essentially will do is load uh just

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:26.910
this token, but also the 27,000 tokens

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:29.110
that are pre-injected as a system prompt

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.230
in this session. And so theoretically,

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.470
once this is done giving you an answer,

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.430
it has consumed a total of something

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:38.110
like 28,000 tokens in full. And so after

00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:39.710
that, you can just go back to account

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.190
and usage and just see if this ticker

00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:44.350
has moved for you or not. If it didn't,

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:46.070
then that's good, because that means

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.470
that your skills are probably not yet at

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.510
the point that they are materially

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.910
affecting the usage limits that you have

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.310
set based on your current plan. So you

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:57.070
can see for me, it didn't really budge

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:58.750
because in the larger scheme of things,

00:02:58.760 --> 00:03:00.830
27,000 tokens, even though that seems

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:02.870
like a lot, is not actually that big.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:05.190
And so there you go, that is skills from

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:07.430
A to Z. My challenge to you is today,

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.070
save a skill and make a few skills

00:03:09.080 --> 00:03:10.790
yourself. There's probably a lot of

00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:12.910
workflows that you can automate already

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.790
just by talking to CloudCode, and by the

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.670
end of that session, just having it save

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.350
that skill for you so that you can use

00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.040
it the next time that you do that task.
